    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d798">

                <pb facs="0807" n="803" sameAs="frus:frus1939v03/pg803"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.002/808: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Chefoo</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Roberts</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chefoo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-01-14T10:00:00+08:00">January 14,
                            1939—10 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 14—7 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3. 1. Chefoo Harbor Office recently organized by the Japanese Navy announced that
                    effective January 15 it will take over from the Chinese Maritime Customs: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“(1), Supervision of pilotage; (2), assignment of berths; (3), control
                            harbor and all vessels entering and leaving it; (4), supervision of
                            quarantine; (5), notifications concerning the harbor; (6), communication
                            with vessels.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>2. Masters of vessels are required to deliver on arriving to harbor boarding
                    officer arrival report, passenger list, crew list and import <pb facs="0808"
                        n="804" xml:id="pg804"/> manifest and on departing to the Chefoo Harbor
                    Office clearance application, passenger list and export manifest.</p>
                <p>3. Shanghai please inform Commander in Chief.<anchor n="39" xml:id="d798-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Repeated to Peiping, Tsingtao and Chungking.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Roberts</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d798-f1" n="39" xml:id="d798-f1-content">
                <p>Adm. Harry E. Yarnell, U. S. Asiatic Fleet.</p>
